I scratch my head, growing thinner and paler,
Almost too thin for the pin of my hat.

I left home young and return in old age;
My accent unchanged, my hair turned thin and grey.
My children, whom I meet, do not know who I am;
Smiling, they ask: 'Dear stranger, from where do you come?'
